### 4. .plans/GOMAD_MILESTONES.md 'Open findings' D25 bullet at HEAD
- **`TestDescribeTaskQueueEnhanced_ReportFlags`** (versioning suite) fails deterministically ("poller
  info should not be reported") because of a server bug: the enhanced-mode `DescribeTaskQueue`
  response cache in `service/matching/matching_engine.go` is keyed by build ID and task-queue type
  only (`dtq_enhanced:<buildId>.<type>`), so a reachability-only request inside the cache TTL is
  served the previous response's pollers. Virtual time puts the second call in the same instant
  as the first, so the hit is certain. The user approved a required production
  correction in [D25](../.flow/tasks/fn-105-gomad-follow-ups-deferred-scope.25.md)
  on 2026-09-30, with regression evidence and a dedicated production review.
  The suite's `target_failure` expectation cites this finding until verification
  supports updating the disposition.

### 4b. same bullet now
- **`TestDescribeTaskQueueEnhanced_ReportFlags`** (versioning suite) is resolved in the working
  tree under [D25](../.flow/tasks/fn-105-gomad-follow-ups-deferred-scope.25.md), by two
  corrections. The server bug: the enhanced-mode `DescribeTaskQueue` cache in
  `service/matching/matching_engine.go` was keyed by build ID and task-queue type only, so a
  reachability-only request inside the cache TTL was served the previous response's pollers
  ("poller info should not be reported"); the key now carries the poller and stats flags, with
  unit regressions and a dedicated production review. The test's readiness wait: it accepted
  the worker's poller under either task-queue type while the last request asserts one poller
  under each, so with the server fix the test failed there instead ("only one poller info
  should be reported") on both seeds. Every call runs in one virtual instant, the 1ns cache TTL
  the suite configures never elapses, and the incomplete first response was served again;
  natively the same race is only hidden by wall time passing. The wait now requires the poller
  under both types, with no assertion changed. `TestVersioningFunctionalSuite` then qualifies
  on seeds 11 and 17 with two repetitions each on darwin/arm64 (2026-09-30, no choice trace or
  success replay, as its manifest entry specifies), and its `target_failure` expectation is
  removed. linux/amd64 was not run.

